TASK
1. STRUCTURE — the blueprint must contain, as ## headings: Executive summary; The engagement — context and scope; Where you are today; The opportunity; How this makes money; The product, module by module; What we'd build first; What success looks like. Flag any missing or empty.
2. CONSISTENCY — the document must not contradict the layers: every module named in the document exists in the module list and vice versa; the scope obeys the register (a capability engagement never redesigns the whole business); the executive summary's claims appear in the body.
3. COVERAGE — the structured layers live ALONGSIDE the document (they render as their own sections and pages); their absence from the document text is CORRECT and never a finding. A coverage finding exists only when a layer's COUNT above is zero: no journey stages, no scoreboard rows, no risks, or no quick wins.

Respond with ONLY this JSON shape, no markdown fences, no commentary:

